{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "B8iy2Yeeyr12zZEAu",
	"notes": "A full Astropath of the Adeptus Astra Telepathica: Beta-grade (Psyker Talent 4), soul-bound to the Emperor's light and blinded in the binding ritual, trained in Telepathy as their core discipline (which includes Astrotelepathy, their signature interstellar-relay power). Built on the Thaumatology: Sorcery model (see framework.md and Imperium/Traits/Psykers and the Warp.adq): Psyker (Talent) sharpens skills; Warp Empowerment gates which powers can be known. This loadout's costliest known power is Dominate (full modified cost 35), so it needs Warp Empowerment level 3 (cap 40), buying only what the Telepathy list needs. Beta grade on the Assignment table (Warp Empowerment's notes) is level 18 (cap 190), sized for holding an attack power at lore strength; Astropaths have no attack powers here, so the extra levels would buy nothing. A GM who wants this Astropath to push Psychic Scream or Terrify higher, or to learn an attack power, should raise Warp Empowerment toward level 18.\nPoint math: 60 (attributes: IQ 40 + Will 20) + 10 (Unusual Background) + 40 (Psyker 4) + 40 (Warp Empowerment 3) - 15 (Sanctioned Psyker) - 55 (Soulbinding) + 8 (Witch-sight, 10 base x 0.8 Warp Sorcery) + 119 (Telepathy discipline at default starting levels: Mind Probe/Dominate alt 35+3, Psychic Scream 12, Terrify 28, Mental Interrogation 21, Astrotelepathy 20) + 19 (skills) = 226 points. The Blindness and Soulbinding costs pull the raw total down hard, which is intentional — an Astropath trades an enormous amount for their gift, offset here by strong mental attributes and a powerful, wide-ranging Telepathy list; total lands inside framework.md's \"Elite human (200-350)\" tier. GCS will compute the exact final total from the included traits' own modifiers; treat the figures above as this template's design-time estimate, not a promise of GCS's rounding.\n",
	"traits": [
