		{
			"id": "TuROSuSrssR4vmMH8",
			"name": "Soulbinding (Astropathic Choir)",
			"local_notes": "Lore: To become an Astropath, a Sanctioned psyker undergoes the soul-binding ritual: their eyes are burned out and their mind is bound, in a small part, to the Emperor's own psychic light on the Astronomican, so that their thoughts can be found and carried across interstellar distances. They are permanently blind and permanently, irrevocably in the Emperor's and the Imperium's service from that day on. This is standard background across Dark Heresy/Rogue Trader's Astropath material and referenced throughout Black Library whenever an Astropathic Choir appears (e.g. the Horus Heresy's Astropaths aboard Legion flagships).\n\nDesign: Blindness (Basic B140, -50) is the dominant cost; it is not mitigated mechanically here (their remaining \"sight\" is represented by Witch-sight and their Telepathy powers, not a vision substitute). Mindlink to the Astronomican/the Emperor's light (Basic Mindlink, a specific \"person,\" 5 points) is a genuine benefit — it is how they are found and relayed across the void. Sense of Duty to the Imperium of Man (a very-large-group Sense of Duty, -10, Basic's tier below \"entire race\") completes the package. Net -55.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Physical",
				"Mental",
				"Psyker",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tNEt3Qh_3fz_ABX8i",
					"name": "Blindness",
					"reference": "B140",
					"local_notes": "Lore: See parent trait.\n\nDesign: See parent trait.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
