					"base_points": 30
				},
				{
					"id": "t1EZYv80lJTij-bSY",
					"name": "Astrotelepathy",
					"local_notes": "Lore: The astropath's signature act: sending and receiving thought across interstellar distances, relayed choir to choir and, ultimately, through the Astronomican itself. Astropaths who fail badly during a transmission are a recurring Black Library beat (burned out, driven mad, or lost with the ship's Geller field).\n\nDesign: Base 20 points for a mental send-and-receive package is this project's own baseline (Basic's exact per-range-step Telecommunication costs are not confidently recalled, so this figure is fixed for internal consistency rather than cited to a page); Increased Range at the highest tabled step (+60%) for interstellar reach, Preparation Required (-20%, a ritual trance), and the Severe Perils tier for the real danger of transmitting through the warp. Net +60-20-20-20=0%. Full modified cost: 20 x 1.0 = 20 points; needs only Warp Empowerment level 1 (cap 20) — cheap in raw points despite the interstellar range, since Increased Range's +60% roughly cancels the Preparation Required/Warp Sorcery/Severe Perils discounts; the real cost of Astrotelepathy is the Severe Perils roll, not the point price.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Psyker",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "m8aVVWSwbBGsH2Frm",
							"name": "Increased Range x100",
							"cost_adj": "+60%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mVHNnC1S4NLhZWsPf",
							"name": "Preparation Required",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "m0LjpNTgzd5qe3WpI",
							"name": "Warp Sorcery",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "m3MUB4FAnCfE0a_KV",
							"name": "Perils of the Warp (Severe)",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 20
				}
			]
		}
	],
	"skills": [
		{
			"id": "sDkxqdiqVX6wBolww",
			"name": "Psyniscience",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The trained (or instinctive) sense of \"something wrong\" in a presence, place, or object touched by the warp — a chill in a corridor, a servitor's dead eyes going wrong. Named for the Dark Heresy/Only War skill of the same purpose (Psyniscience), used here for calibration only; the GURPS build is original.\n\nDesign: New skill per framework.md (\"New skills only when nothing fits\"). Per/H with no default: nobody can roll it untrained. Characters with a Psyker Talent (see the psyker power library, not part of this file) get it at a discount per that trait's rules. An unaugmented human without any psychic Talent has nothing latent to sense with and must buy it as an unusual background purchase, if a GM allows it at all; most unaugmented Imperial citizens simply never take this skill.",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Psionic"
			],
			"difficulty": "per/h",
			"points": 8
		},
